<title>USA: Scholastic Corp sets $125 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>Scholastic Corp sets $125 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Scholastic Corp was priced on Wednesday, according to lead manager Goldman Sachs &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>BORROWER SCHOLASTIC CORP</p>
<p>AMT $125 MLN	 COUPON 7.00 PCT   MATURITY 12/15/2003</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.747  FIRST PAY DATE N.A.</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S BAA2  YIELD  7.046 PCT  PAY FREQ	 N.A.</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P BBB	 SPREAD 70 BP	CALLABLE	 NO</p>
<p>UNDERLYING: A BLEND OF THE AUGUST 2003 AND FEBRUARY 2004 U.S. TREASURY NOTE.</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1678</p>
